{
  "description": "BTPS 1.2 details refresh, on an active trust in either direction. Each side fetches only the details it already holds by that trust. `DETAILS_CHANGED` tells the other side which of its details changed, `DETAILS_REQ` asks for some, optionally naming the notice in `relatesTo`, and `DETAILS_RES` answers a request named in `relatesTo`, its values keyed by name and always encrypted to the requester. A notice's or request's document holds no values, only an optional `message`, a 1.2 note. Each carries `details`, the `detail:` names, on its envelope, signed and readable; all three are 1.2.0 only. A response may answer part of a request. `envelopes` are checked by the transporter schema. `held` cases are checked by `detailsProblem(artifact, record, sentRequest)`: `record` is the receiver's trust record (`status` and `permissions: { requested, granted, detailsHeld, detailsShared }`) and `sentRequest` the `DETAILS_REQ` a response names, as the receiver sent it, or null when it sent none. A notice names only details the receiver holds (`detailsHeld`), a request only details the answerer shares (`detailsShared`, else BTP_ERROR_DETAILS_NOT_HELD), and a response only names its request asked for and the receiver holds; where a response's document is readable (as when opened), it holds a value for every name, and no others. Here the vendor asked for the trust and the client granted its legal name and email.",
